{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-42159" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+7y=4 \\\\ 6x+42y=24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a364eba581ece0637381aa6c11db654bf2490b8ce3dfd916e5e9506ed81b326"} {"question" "q-42159" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 42 & -24\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 42 & 24\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-6){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+7y=4 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+7y=4.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=4-7y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=4-7y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4-7y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a364eba581ece0637381aa6c11db654bf2490b8ce3dfd916e5e9506ed81b326"} {"question" "q-42159" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a5075986389a705f9a1167392eeca9fd79bef4e22632515d2329da419fc6c2ca"} {"question" "q-42159" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a364eba581ece0637381aa6c11db654bf2490b8ce3dfd916e5e9506ed81b326"} {"question" "q-42159" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4+7y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4-7y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6-9y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7-4y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["text" "No solution"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a364eba581ece0637381aa6c11db654bf2490b8ce3dfd916e5e9506ed81b326"} {"question" "q-42159" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4-7y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a364eba581ece0637381aa6c11db654bf2490b8ce3dfd916e5e9506ed81b326"} {"question" "q-73524" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -16 & 8 \\\\ -3 & 12 & -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a364eba581ece0637381aa6c11db654bf2490b8ce3dfd916e5e9506ed81b326"} {"question" "q-73524" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -16 & 8 \\\\ -3 & 12 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 12 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a364eba581ece0637381aa6c11db654bf2490b8ce3dfd916e5e9506ed81b326"} {"question" "q-73524" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a5075986389a705f9a1167392eeca9fd79bef4e22632515d2329da419fc6c2ca"} {"question" "q-73524" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a364eba581ece0637381aa6c11db654bf2490b8ce3dfd916e5e9506ed81b326"} {"question" "q-73524" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -16 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 12\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & -16 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a364eba581ece0637381aa6c11db654bf2490b8ce3dfd916e5e9506ed81b326"} {"question" "q-73524" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a364eba581ece0637381aa6c11db654bf2490b8ce3dfd916e5e9506ed81b326"} {"question" "q-73743" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a364eba581ece0637381aa6c11db654bf2490b8ce3dfd916e5e9506ed81b326"} {"question" "q-73743" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 6 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a364eba581ece0637381aa6c11db654bf2490b8ce3dfd916e5e9506ed81b326"} {"question" "q-73743" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a5075986389a705f9a1167392eeca9fd79bef4e22632515d2329da419fc6c2ca"} {"question" "q-73743" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a364eba581ece0637381aa6c11db654bf2490b8ce3dfd916e5e9506ed81b326"} {"question" "q-73743" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a364eba581ece0637381aa6c11db654bf2490b8ce3dfd916e5e9506ed81b326"} {"question" "q-73743" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a364eba581ece0637381aa6c11db654bf2490b8ce3dfd916e5e9506ed81b326"} {"question" "q-73752" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-6y=10 \\\\ -x+3y=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a364eba581ece0637381aa6c11db654bf2490b8ce3dfd916e5e9506ed81b326"} {"question" "q-73752" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 & 10 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 & 10 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-3y=5 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-3y=5.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=5+3y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=5+3y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5+3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a364eba581ece0637381aa6c11db654bf2490b8ce3dfd916e5e9506ed81b326"} {"question" "q-73752" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a5075986389a705f9a1167392eeca9fd79bef4e22632515d2329da419fc6c2ca"} {"question" "q-73752" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a364eba581ece0637381aa6c11db654bf2490b8ce3dfd916e5e9506ed81b326"} {"question" "q-73752" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3+5y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3-5y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5+3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5-3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["text" "No solution"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a364eba581ece0637381aa6c11db654bf2490b8ce3dfd916e5e9506ed81b326"} {"question" "q-73752" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5+3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a364eba581ece0637381aa6c11db654bf2490b8ce3dfd916e5e9506ed81b326"} {"question" "q-130924" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2x+8y=4 \\\\ -3x+12y=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a364eba581ece0637381aa6c11db654bf2490b8ce3dfd916e5e9506ed81b326"} {"question" "q-130924" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 8 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 10 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 8 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 12 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 12 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-4y=-2 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-4y=-2.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=4y-2,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=4y-2 \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4y-2 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a364eba581ece0637381aa6c11db654bf2490b8ce3dfd916e5e9506ed81b326"} {"question" "q-130924" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a5075986389a705f9a1167392eeca9fd79bef4e22632515d2329da419fc6c2ca"} {"question" "q-130924" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a364eba581ece0637381aa6c11db654bf2490b8ce3dfd916e5e9506ed81b326"} {"question" "q-130924" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2-4y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2y-4 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4y+2 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4y-2 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["text" "No solution"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a364eba581ece0637381aa6c11db654bf2490b8ce3dfd916e5e9506ed81b326"} {"question" "q-130924" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4y-2 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a364eba581ece0637381aa6c11db654bf2490b8ce3dfd916e5e9506ed81b326"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1653 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
